# Epic Developer Community

> Epic Games' hub for developers: documentation, learning resources, forums, and community content for Unreal Engine and Epic technologies.

dev.epicgames.com is the canonical home for Epic's developer documentation and learning material. If you need Unreal Engine documentation, API reference, tutorials, or the Epic Online Services SDK reference, it is here rather than on the product marketing sites.

The sitemap linked at the end of this file covers only a small part of the domain. The documentation, community, learning, and Developer Portal areas are served by separate systems with their own indexes, so the curated links below are a more reliable entry point than the sitemap.

## Documentation

- [Unreal Engine documentation](https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation/en-us/unreal-engine): Official Unreal Engine documentation and C++/Blueprint API reference.
- [All documentation](https://dev.epicgames.com/documentation): Documentation index across Unreal Engine, MetaHuman, and other Epic technologies.
- [Epic Online Services SDK docs](https://dev.epicgames.com/docs): EOS SDK reference and integration guides for crossplay, accounts, and anti-cheat.

## Learning and community

- [Epic Developer Community](https://dev.epicgames.com/community): Tutorials, courses, learning paths, and community-contributed guides.
- [Unreal Engine learning](https://dev.epicgames.com/community/unreal-engine/learning): Structured Unreal Engine courses and learning paths.
- [Unreal Engine forums](https://forums.unrealengine.com/): Official support and discussion forums for Unreal Engine.

## Developer tools and accounts

- [Support](https://dev.epicgames.com/support): Developer support routes and contact options.

## Epic technologies

- [Unreal Engine](https://www.unrealengine.com/): Product site for downloads, licensing terms, and industry use cases.
- [Epic Online Services](https://onlineservices.epicgames.com/): Free cross-platform backend services for multiplayer games.
- [MetaHuman](https://www.metahuman.com/): Tools for creating and animating photorealistic digital humans.
- [Fab](https://www.fab.com/): Epic's marketplace for 3D models, materials, and plugins.

